---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Create a High-Converting Landing Page (2026 Guide) | PixelPage Blog"
  description="A practical checklist for building landing pages that convert — covering headline structure, CTA placement, trust signals, speed, and testing."
>
  <Nav />

  <article class="pt-32 pb-24 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 font-sans">
    <header class="mb-10 text-center">
      <span class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-violet-400 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-violet-500/10 border border-violet-500/20">
        Conversion Strategy
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mt-4 mb-4">
        How to Create a High-Converting Landing Page
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-xs text-gray-400 pb-6 border-b border-white/10">
        <span>By PixelPage Strategy Team</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>July 26, 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>5 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300 space-y-6 leading-relaxed pt-2">
      <p class="text-base text-gray-200 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        A landing page has one job: get the visitor to take a single targeted action. Here's a practical checklist to build one that converts consistently.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight pt-4">The 8-Point High-Conversion Checklist</h2>

      <ol class="space-y-4 list-decimal list-inside text-gray-300">
        <li>
          <strong>Write one clear headline.</strong> Your headline should state the specific outcome, not a vague benefit. <em>"Write cold emails that get 40% reply rates"</em> converts better than <em>"Better email marketing."</em> Specificity builds trust instantly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Match the page to the ad.</strong> If someone clicks an ad about a discount, they should land on a page about that discount — not your generic homepage. Message match is a critical conversion factor.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Keep the CTA visible and repeated.</strong> Don't bury your call-to-action below three scrolls. Repeat it after your hero section, after your features grid, and again in the final footer CTA.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cut fluff, sharpen persuasion.</strong> Every sentence should either remove a doubt or build desire. Short, punchy sections almost always outperform dense paragraphs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Place proof near decision points.</strong> Testimonials, client logos, or specific numbers ("500+ agencies") work best right next to your CTA button.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Check compliance before launch.</strong> Vague guarantees or exaggerated claims get pages flagged by Meta and Google Ads — costing ad spend and account status.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Test variants, don't guess.</strong> Even small headline or CTA changes can shift conversion rates significantly. Always launch with at least two variants (Control vs Challenger) running.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Keep load times sub-second.</strong> Slow pages lose visitors before they even see your offer. Clean, semantic HTML beats bloated drag-and-drop page builder code.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="pt-2">
        Doing all of this manually takes days. Multi-agent AI tools like PixelPage handle copy, modern design tokens, ad compliance scanning, and A/B variant generation automatically from a single prompt.
      </p>

      <div class="pt-8 border-t border-white/10 mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Ready to build high-converting pages automatically?</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">Generate on-brand landing pages with built-in A/B testing.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/chat" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-bold text-xs bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-fuchsia-500 text-white shadow-lg">
          Start Free Generator Studio →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
